---
# Purpose
Shows organisation owners and admins how to start their own org brain and
keep an eye on it, and states the isolation rule in plain words.

# Sanitization
Rewrite-only from the Account Admin Org brain tab and the deploy flow.
Quotes only on-screen text (status lines, button names, group names). No
rings, hosts, ports, services, request ids or release numbers; "the ring"
appears only inside quoted on-screen lines.

# Gotchas (keep these true)
- The panel is shown to org owners/admins (and greatVibe admin staff), not
  members or guests.
- Deploy and reset need passkey verification; the new-org deploy does not.
- The tab switches to the hosted view by itself (it checks for up to about
  150 s after a deploy) since 2026-11-14; before that it waited for the
  minute refresh.
- A new brain: 0 live turns, CPU "no samples" for the first minute, Deep ask
  Off (no model answers for new brains yet).
- Process restart is staff-only and deliberately not described here.
- Isolation: the organisation comes from the node, so trusted meshes and
  members of two organisations never reach another org's brain from the
  wrong node.

# Change History
